From: Codex folio backport <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] E404 folio G2.5e: Add FGP_STABLE (upstream 89/90)

__filemap_get_folio() learns FGP_STABLE, which waits for the folio to be
stable, and grab_cache_page_write_begin() stops calling
wait_for_stable_page() itself and asks for it through the flag instead.
folio_wait_stable() is added in mm/page-writeback.c next to
wait_for_stable_page(), which becomes its wrapper.

Divergences from upstream, all deliberate:

  - FGP_STABLE is 0x00000200, the upstream value, and not the next free bit
    in this tree.  Upstream has FGP_HEAD at 0x00000080 and FGP_ENTRY at
    0x00000100, and neither exists here: the E404 xarray holds only head
    pages, so there is no multipage entry for FGP_HEAD to select and no
    shadow/swap entry for FGP_ENTRY to hand back.  Leaving the two bits
    unused costs nothing, keeps the numbering identical to 5.16, and makes
    it impossible for a flag added here later to collide with a value
    copied from upstream.

  - The FGP_STABLE branch goes straight before the no_page: label.  Upstream
    puts it after the FGP_WRITE/page_is_idle() branch, which the E404
    version of this function does not have, so there is nothing between the
    FGP_ACCESSED branch and no_page: for it to follow.

  - grab_cache_page_write_begin() keeps its own symbol and its
    EXPORT_SYMBOL.  Upstream moves it to mm/folio-compat.c, which this
    tree does not have.  It is not listed in android/abi_gki_aarch64_qcom,
    so unlike pagecache_get_page() there is no ABI promise forcing it, but
    the vendor filesystems in this tree do call it, so it stays a real
    exported function rather than becoming a static inline.

  - noinline goes on pagecache_get_page() in mm/filemap.c.  Upstream puts
    it in mm/folio-compat.c for the same reason it has there: to keep a
    compatibility wrapper out of the callers' hot path.  That function is
    already a real function since G2.5d, for the ABI reason documented
    there, so the attribute lands on the same definition.

  - folio_wait_stable() keeps the PageWriteback() pre-check that
    wait_for_stable_page() got from wait_on_page_writeback(), spelled as
    folio_test_writeback().  It is not redundant: without it every caller
    would take the page lock of the waitqueue only to find nothing to
    wait for.

E404's grab_cache_page_write_begin() was byte-for-byte the same as the 5.16
version this patch rewrites, so that hunk ports directly.  The wait still
happens before the page is returned to the caller, which is where the
explicit wait_for_stable_page() used to run.

The rest of the folio series is untouched: find_get_entry() from G2.5c
keeps its wrapper, the G2.5a allocation path and the G2.5b insertion path
are unchanged, and no caller outside mm/filemap.c is converted.

diff --git a/include/linux/pagemap.h b/include/linux/pagemap.h
index 3ac02b1..e494b8f 100644
--- a/include/linux/pagemap.h
+++ b/include/linux/pagemap.h
@@ -313,6 +313,17 @@ pgoff_t page_cache_prev_miss(struct address_space *mapping,
 #define FGP_NOFS		0x00000010
 #define FGP_NOWAIT		0x00000020
 #define FGP_FOR_MMAP		0x00000040
+/*
+ * Upstream patch 89/90.  The value is the upstream one, 0x00000200, and
+ * not the next free bit in this tree.  Upstream has %FGP_HEAD at
+ * 0x00000080 and %FGP_ENTRY at 0x00000100, neither of which exists
+ * here: the E404 xarray holds only head pages, so there is no multipage
+ * entry for %FGP_HEAD to select and no shadow/swap entry for
+ * %FGP_ENTRY to hand back.  Leaving the two bits unused costs nothing and
+ * keeps the numbering identical to 5.16, so a flag added here later
+ * cannot collide with a value taken from upstream.
+ */
+#define FGP_STABLE		0x00000200
 
 struct folio *__filemap_get_folio(struct address_space *mapping, pgoff_t index,
 		int fgp_flags, gfp_t gfp);
@@ -795,6 +806,7 @@ static inline __sched void wait_on_page_writeback(struct page *page)
 
 extern void end_page_writeback(struct page *page);
 void folio_end_writeback(struct folio *folio);
+void folio_wait_stable(struct folio *folio);
 void wait_for_stable_page(struct page *page);
 
 void page_endio(struct page *page, bool is_write, int err);
diff --git a/mm/filemap.c b/mm/filemap.c
index 414896f..3a93ad2 100644
--- a/mm/filemap.c
+++ b/mm/filemap.c
@@ -1969,6 +1969,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(find_lock_entry);
  * * %FGP_WRITE - The page will be written
  * * %FGP_NOFS - __GFP_FS will get cleared in gfp mask
  * * %FGP_NOWAIT - Don't get blocked by page lock
+ * * %FGP_STABLE - Wait for the folio to be stable (finished writeback).
  *
  * If %FGP_LOCK or %FGP_CREAT are specified then the function may sleep even
  * if the %GFP flags specified for %FGP_CREAT are atomic.
@@ -2025,6 +2026,12 @@ repeat:
 	if (folio && (fgp_flags & FGP_ACCESSED))
 		folio_mark_accessed(folio);
 
+	/* O folio nao e NULL aqui: o branch acima so salta para no_page se for.
+	 * O upstream poe este pedaco depois do ramo FGP_WRITE/page_is_idle(),
+	 * que esta arvore nao tem. */
+	if (fgp_flags & FGP_STABLE)
+		folio_wait_stable(folio);
+
 no_page:
 	if (!folio && (fgp_flags & FGP_CREAT)) {
 		int err;
@@ -2077,6 +2084,9 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(__filemap_get_folio);
  * E404 has neither the flag nor the multi-page xarray entries those handle,
  * so the head page is always the right answer here.
  */
+/* noinline vem do patch 89/90, onde fica em mm/folio-compat.c: mantem este
+ * wrapper de compatibilidade fora das linhas quentes de quem so quer uma page. */
+noinline
 struct page *pagecache_get_page(struct address_space *mapping, pgoff_t offset,
 		int fgp_flags, gfp_t cache_gfp_mask)
 {
@@ -3563,22 +3573,26 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(generic_file_direct_write);
 /*
  * Find or create a page at the given pagecache position. Return the locked
  * page. This function is specifically for buffered writes.
+ *
+ * Upstream patch 89/90: the wait for a stable page happens inside
+ * __filemap_get_folio() behind FGP_STABLE, so that any caller of
+ * filemap_get_folio() can ask for it.  It ran at the same point, before
+ * the page was returned.
+ *
+ * This stays a real function with its EXPORT_SYMBOL, not a static inline,
+ * because the vendor filesystems in this tree call it.  It is not in
+ * android/abi_gki_aarch64_qcom, but it is a live exported entry point.
  */
 struct page *grab_cache_page_write_begin(struct address_space *mapping,
 					pgoff_t index, unsigned flags)
 {
-	struct page *page;
-	int fgp_flags = FGP_LOCK|FGP_WRITE|FGP_CREAT;
+	int fgp_flags = FGP_LOCK|FGP_WRITE|FGP_CREAT|FGP_STABLE;
 
 	if (flags & AOP_FLAG_NOFS)
 		fgp_flags |= FGP_NOFS;
 
-	page = pagecache_get_page(mapping, index, fgp_flags,
+	return pagecache_get_page(mapping, index, fgp_flags,
 			mapping_gfp_mask(mapping));
-	if (page)
-		wait_for_stable_page(page);
-
-	return page;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(grab_cache_page_write_begin);
 
diff --git a/mm/page-writeback.c b/mm/page-writeback.c
index c0b978b..dc1e9f9 100644
--- a/mm/page-writeback.c
+++ b/mm/page-writeback.c
@@ -2816,16 +2816,34 @@ int __test_set_page_writeback(struct page *page, bool keep_write)
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(__test_set_page_writeback);
 
 /**
- * wait_for_stable_page() - wait for writeback to finish, if necessary.
- * @page:	The page to wait on.
+ * folio_wait_stable - wait for writeback to finish, if necessary.
+ * @folio: The folio to wait on.
  *
- * This function determines if the given page is related to a backing device
- * that requires page contents to be held stable during writeback.  If so, then
- * it will wait for any pending writeback to complete.
+ * This function determines if the given folio is related to a backing device
+ * that requires page contents to be held stable during writeback.  If so, it
+ * will wait for any pending writeback to complete.
+ *
+ * Upstream patch 89/90.  The body is E404's wait_for_stable_page() with the
+ * page replaced by the folio it heads.  The PageWriteback() pre-check of
+ * wait_on_page_writeback() is kept, spelled as folio_test_writeback(): it is
+ * not redundant, it avoids taking the page lock of the waitqueue only to find
+ * out that there is nothing to wait for.
+ */
+void folio_wait_stable(struct folio *folio)
+{
+	if (bdi_cap_stable_pages_required(inode_to_bdi(folio->mapping->host)) &&
+	    folio_test_writeback(folio))
+		folio_wait_bit(folio, PG_writeback);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(folio_wait_stable);
+
+/*
+ * Compatibility wrapper for callers that were not converted to folios
+ * (upstream keeps wait_for_stable_page() in mm/filemap.c and lets this one
+ * disappear later; this tree has no mm/folio-compat.c to move it to).
  */
 void wait_for_stable_page(struct page *page)
 {
-	if (bdi_cap_stable_pages_required(inode_to_bdi(page->mapping->host)))
-		wait_on_page_writeback(page);
+	folio_wait_stable(page_folio(page));
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(wait_for_stable_page);
